.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt LOGD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm logd
.Nd RavenBSD system log server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar console=0
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dq log:
scheme.
Opening
.Pa log:<name>
and writing appends a record of the form
.D1 Ar seconds . Ns Ar millis Ar name : Ar message
to a fixed 64 KiB ring.
The writer name is the path suffix; opening
.Pa log:
uses
.Dq log .
Reads return the retained text from a per-handle cursor starting at the oldest byte, so a slow
reader sees the retained tail after an overwrite.
.Pp
Records are limited to 1 KiB; a longer message is truncated and ends with
.Dq ... .
Each record is also copied to the console with
.Xr debug_write 2
unless the argument
.Ar console=0
is present.
.Pp
The log is in memory only and is lost when
.Nm
restarts.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/logd.toml
Service manifest.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysd 8 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
